* Marshall JCM800 2203 preamp (V1a, V1b, V2a, V2b cathode follower, tone stack, master),
* transcribed from the factory schematic. Element order is part of the contract: the solver's
* floating-point sums follow it, and the parity tests compare against the original Rust build.
*
* Units: k M, m u n p. Node "0" is ground. See engine/include/sas/netlist.h for the format.

* Node numbering (golden DC dumps list nodes in this order); the Low-jack nodes come last.
.nodes x b1 in g1 p1 k1 vt vp w p1b k1b g2 g2a p2a k2a k2b m t w3 n1 n2 wm y c3n lowin gin lowsrc

* Rail (node X): driven from the power amp at run time; 410 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 410
* The guitar (or the pedal in front of the amp) behind a variable source resistance.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k

* Supply decoupling: R8 and the two 50 uF sections of C21.
R R8 x b1 10k
C C21B b1 0 50u
C C21A x 0 50u

* Input and V1a.
R R2 in 0 1M
R R3 in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 ECC83
R R4 b1 p1 100k
R R1 k1 0 2.7k
C C1 k1 0 0.68u
C C2 p1 k1 100p

* Coupling to the volume network. SW_C3 is the Low jack's normally-closed contact; with the
* guitar in the Low jack the guitar enters at the volume network and C3 is opened.
C C3 p1 c3n 0.022u
R SW_C3 c3n vt 1
S VLOW lowsrc 1 0
R RSRC_LOW lowsrc lowin 7k
R SW_LOW lowin vt 1e12
R R5 vt vp 470k
C C4 vt vp 470p
C C5 vp w 1n
R VR1T vp w 1
R VR1B w 0 1

* V1b.
T V1B w p1b k1b ECC83
R R7 b1 p1b 100k
R R6 k1b 0 10k

* C7 into V2a's divider.
C C7 p1b g2 0.022u
R R10 g2 g2a 470k
C C8 g2 g2a 470p
R R11 g2a 0 470k

* V2a and the V2b cathode follower (plate on the rail).
T V2A g2a p2a k2a ECC83
R R12 x p2a 100k
R R9 k2a 0 820
T V2B p2a x k2b ECC83
R R13 k2b 0 100k

* Tone stack.
R R15 k2b m 33k
C C10 k2b t 470p
R VR3T t w3 1
R VR3B w3 n1 1
C C11 m n1 0.022u
R VR5 n1 n2 1
R VR4T n2 wm 1
R VR4B wm 0 1
C C12 m wm 0.022u

* Master volume and the load it sees.
R VR2T w3 y 1
R VR2B y 0 1
R RMASTERLOAD y 0 1M
